    description: "Pet wash station engineering means waterproof rooms, hair-proof drainage, and safe tempered water. Here is what commercial pet wash design really requires.",
    h1: "What Does Pet Wash Station Engineering Design Really Require?",
    answer: "Pet wash station engineering is the design of the wet rooms — in groomers, daycares, kennels, and retail — where dogs get bathed. The engineering centers on waterproof room construction, drainage that handles hair and high water volume, tempered water delivery that cannot scald, and slip-resistant surfaces for wet dogs and wet staff. I have seen wash rooms that worked beautifully for years and ones where the drywall melted, the drains clogged monthly, and the floor stayed wet all day. Every one of those failures was a design decision: the wrong wall finish, no hair interception, no floor pitch. Wash rooms are small, but they punish bad engineering daily.",
    directAnswer: "Pet wash station engineering is the MEP design of commercial dog-bathing rooms. It covers waterproof wall and floor assemblies, hair-intercepting drainage pitched to drains, tempered and scald-protected water, GFCI electrical, and slip-resistant surfaces — plus ventilation that clears the constant humidity a wash room generates.",
