        body: "Self-serve dog wash engineering is the MEP design of unattended coin- or card-operated dog-bathing stations. It covers vandal-resistant plumbing and equipment, waterproof room construction, hair-intercepting drainage, tempered water, payment-system power and data, and ventilation — all designed for unsupervised public use.\n\nThe design philosophy is simple: assume the hardest possible use and no supervision. A staffed groomer can nurse a finicky drain or a temperamental card reader; a self-serve station at 10 p.m. cannot. I specify commercial-grade components throughout, conceal what can be concealed, waterproof everything, and make the maintenance path so simple that one person with a key can reset the whole station in minutes.",
